  "result": "**Final verdict: `OK`** (3 of 6 gate runs used).\n\nWhat I wrote:\n\n- **Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_413_2.lean`) — binder class `ru_aggregate v \"DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle\"`; applicability `.rises (drv_motion_turning v [p.turn_recognition_window, p.heading_change_noise_floor])`; obligation `asm → (100 ft duty)` ∧ `¬asm → (300 ft duty)`, each duty being `yaw_rate > 0 → holdsFor .path d \"v\" (indicator left ∨ arm left)` conjoined with the mirror for a negative rate. The hand is read at the judged observation, outside the window; the two feet figures are the text's own through `Units.feet`.\n- **Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_413_2.lean`) — twelve scenarios on one built carriageway: the six planned names plus six `branch_<n>` that reach the remaining leaves (each district × hand combination with both signal alternatives false, and the pair where 50 m of signal keeps the 100 ft bound but breaks the 300 ft one).\n- **`task_result.md`** — the verdict, each gate run and what changed, and the choices I made.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n1. The gate enforces adapter-producibility that the Core files don't state: a scene's heading must equal the previous heading rotated by its yaw rate over the interval *before* it, and `kin.path_length` must grow by at least the chord between consecutive positions. That drove both failed runs; the final traces turn through the exactly representable unit heading (24/25, 7/25) with the yaw rate as `Units.millidegrees 32520`, so position, velocity, heading and path increment are exact and only the yaw rate carries a 0.0002° rounding.\n2. I declared one narrowing of my own on s1: the hand comes from the *sign* of `kin.yaw_rate`, so an observation whose rate of change of heading is exactly zero has no hand and the duty is not stated there. Everything else I wrote is the record's reading, and the node needed no repair.",
